  "application_type_full": "Lawful development: Proposed use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason\rThe Royal Borough of Kingston upon Thames as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 11.06.2026, the use of the address of existing dwellinghouse by the applicant for a private vehicle hire centre is lawful within the meaning of section 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\rThe private vehicle hire business within the property amounts to the receipt of remote bookings with no parking, picking up or dropping off of customers at the site or comings and goings of customers to the premises. \r\rNo external alterations are proposed, and the nature and scale of the business use would not amount to a material change of use of part or whole of the house. As such, planning permission is not required.\r"
  ],
